# --- Dev DB Refresh Script (.env.refresh) ---
# Used by `pnpm refresh-dev` to sync media from production into your dev env.
# Create a .env.refresh file (gitignored) with these vars:
#
# PROD_S3_BUCKET=lepi-labs-payload-storage
# PROD_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# PROD_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# PROD_S3_REGION=nyc3
# PROD_S3_ENDPOINT=https://nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com
# Optional: override the public URL prefix that appears in media docs
# PROD_S3_PUBLIC_URL=https://nyc3.digitaloceanspaces.com/lepi-labs-payload-storage
#
# The script picks a media sync mode based on which dev storage vars are set:
#
# - S3 -> S3 copy:   set S3_* vars in .env (S3_ENABLED=true) AND PROD_S3_* in .env.refresh.
#                    Prod bucket objects are copied to the dev S3 bucket, and media
#                    URLs are rewritten to the dev bucket's public URL.
#
# - S3 -> local:     set ONLY PROD_S3_* in .env.refresh (leave S3_* unset / S3_ENABLED=false).
#                    Prod bucket objects are downloaded to public/media/ and media URLs
#                    are rewritten to a local prefix (e.g. /api/media/file/<filename>).
#                    This is the recommended mode for local development.
#
# - skipped:        no PROD_S3_* configured — no media is synced.
#
# Optional overrides for local mode:
# MEDIA_LOCAL_DIR=/absolute/path/to/public/media
# MEDIA_LOCAL_URL_PREFIX=/api/media/file
